course: dictionary
lesson: 10039
title: Tern: a seabird on a long journey
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A tern is a seabird. It looks like a small, slim gull, with long pointed wings, a forked tail and often a black cap. Terns dive into the water to catch fish.
explain: Use the words around a new word to work out its meaning. «The Arctic tern makes the longest migration of any animal.» The word migration is new, but the sentence tells you about a bird that flies a very long way each year, so migration must mean a long journey that animals make, often with the seasons.
explain: Tern is a noun, so it names a thing: one tern, two terns. Test your meaning by putting it into a sentence: «A tern dived into the sea to catch a fish.» That makes sense, so you have understood the word.
fact: A tern is a seabird like a small, slim gull.
fact: Terns have long pointed wings and a forked tail, and often a black cap.
fact: Terns dive into water to catch fish.
fact: «Arctic terns fly from the Arctic to the Antarctic and back every year.»
fact: Terns nest on beaches and islands, so walkers must keep away from their nests.
exercise: What is a tern? | A tall tree with forked branches | A type of sand used on beaches | *A seabird like a small, slim gull | A large black fish that lives in rivers
exercise: «Arctic terns fly from the Arctic to the Antarctic and back every year.» What does migration mean here? | *A long journey made each year, often with the seasons | A nest built high on a cliff | A quick swim across a lake | Sleeping all winter in one place
exercise: «The Arctic tern makes the longest migration of any animal.» What does longest tell you? | It never leaves its nest | It is the shortest trip in the world | *It travels further each year than any other animal | It only flies at night
test: «Terns nest on beaches and islands, so walkers must keep away.» Where do terns nest? | Inside tall city buildings | Out in the middle of the ocean, on the water | *On beaches and islands | In deep caves under the ground
test: Find the word in «A tern dived into the water to catch fish» that names the bird. | water | *tern | fish | dived
exam: Tom says a tern is a fish. What is a tern really? | *A seabird like a small, slim gull that dives for fish | A cloud that brings rain | Fish that swim in rivers | A tree with long, pointed leaves
